 ## Retries
 
-Every attempt to capture one pantry order sends the same idempotency key, the one its first attempt used. The gateway
-can report a timeout after it has already charged the card, and it charges again for a new key: in 2024 retries that
-drew a fresh key for each attempt charged 41 members twice.
+The gateway sometimes rejects a retried capture with a "duplicate idempotency key" error. Each capture attempt now
+sends its own idempotency key; see [the capture implementation](../../larder/capture.py) for the retry loop.
+
+## Known limits
+
+The gateway can report a timeout after it has already charged the card, and it charges again for a new key: in 2024
+retries that drew a fresh key for each attempt charged 41 members twice. Using a new key on retries retains this
+risk. If a member is charged twice, follow [Duplicate charge](../runbooks/duplicate-charge.md) to refund the later
+capture.
 
